Ladybird runs a spellcheck only while the page has transient user
activation — so a page can’t start one at will to test words against the
user’s dictionary. Blink puts the same limit on its own checks, for the
same reason: ColdModeSpellCheckRequester::QualifyingEditable() skips a
field when the page lacks transient activation, or when the user didn’t
focus it. And IdleSpellCheckController::RespondToChangedContents() skips
any edit made without transient activation.
